   "conversationId": "2102982971896848875",
   "text": "This is such an important topic. Healthcare price transparency does not exist. \n\nAlways challenge your healthcare bill by asking for an itemized report of the charges and in network allowable. \n\nIf out of network, call the clinic or physician group and ask to negotiate a fair and reasonable payment. \n\nThe insurance companies don’t pay their contractually required payments to physicians or ASCs forcing physicians and surgical centers to go out of network. \n\nPatients are balanced billed because insurance determines that the payment should be $0.01. \n\nClinic and facility claims are submitted to the Independent Dispute Resolution process of the NSA act. We win over 90% of the time. \n\nInsurance companies ignore the win in arbitration and refuse to pay. There reason for not paying:  “the IDR determination is unenforceable, so we don’t need to pay.” \n\nPhysicians sue insurance company to force them to pay. Insurance company loses in court and still refuses to pay IDR win. \n\nInsurance company appeals loss in court. Circuit court judge says insurance company needs to pay.  Insurance company refuses to pay. \n\nInsurance company appeals again.  And the saga goes on for years. \n\nWe acted in good faith receiving no payment while insurance profited from our good will.  The patients are left wondering why the bills are so high. \n\nI am happy to send an itemized bill. \n\nThe hospital never wants you to see their itemized bill. \n\nQuestion every insurance and hospital statement. \n\nThe corruption runs deep. \n\nWE ARE SO TIRED OF THEIR SHENANIGANS.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-24T04:46:26.000Z",
   "type": "quote",
