   "conversationId": "2101175897092919583",
   "text": "Insurance payments equivalent to what I pay my pet groomer are repugnant. \n\nWe frequently see payments of a few hundred dollars for major operations for facility claims at our ASC and even lower professionally. \n\nWe received a payment of $0.01 for an ASC facility payment on a major case that typically reimburses at $60k or more.   \n\nIt’s a 🖕to every physician in private practice. \n\nWhen we appeal the underpayment, it’s denied. \n\nWhen we submit to the IDR, we win every time. \n\nThey have no justification for their payments. They offer none to the arbitrator. \n\nThese are RICO violations.  \n\nThe insurers are purposely paying way below Medicare fee schedules to force practices into unreasonable contracts or to submit to IDR. \n\nOur only recourse is the IDR or bill the patients. \n\nThey then refuse to pay IDR wins.  They blame physicians and MSOs for price gouging. \n\nThey lie, steal, and blame greedy doctors. \n\nA Blue Cross attorney recently argued in court:  “the IDR determination is as good as writing an IOU on a napkin to your mother”.\n\nInsurers are operating in bad faith by agreeing to participate in the IDR process and then not paying when they lose. \n\nThey litigate in court when they lose. \n\nAll we are asking for is fair and reasonable payments.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-19T05:05:46.000Z",
